### Day 9 - JWT Authentication Tests
### Run the app first: mvn spring-boot:run
### Base URL
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080


### 1. Health check - public endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health


### 2. Try to access assets without token - should return 401 Unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/assets


### 3. Register a normal user - should return token with role USER
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Normal User",
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "User@12345"
}


### 4. Login normal user - copy token from response
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "User@12345"
}


### 5. Get assets with USER token - should return 200 OK
### Replace PASTE_USER_TOKEN_HERE with token from login/register response
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/assets
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_USER_TOKEN_HERE


### 6. Try to create asset with USER token - should return 403 Forbidden
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/assets
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_USER_TOKEN_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetTag": "CAM-2026-2001",
  "name": "Logitech Webcam",
  "category": "Camera",
  "serialNumber": "SN-CAM-2001",
  "location": "HQ Level 2"
}


### 7. Login seeded admin user - copy token from response
### Seeded admin credentials: admin@example.com / Admin@12345
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Admin@12345"
}


### 8. Create asset with ADMIN token - should return 201 Created
### Replace PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE with token from admin login response
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/assets
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetTag": "CAM-2026-3001",
  "name": "Logitech Brio Webcam",
  "category": "Camera",
  "serialNumber": "SN-CAM-3001",
  "location": "HQ Level 2"
}


### 9. Login with wrong password - should return 401 Unauthorized
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}


### 10. Register duplicate email - should return 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Duplicate User",
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "User@12345"
}
### ---------------------------
### TICKET API TESTS (DAY 7)
### ---------------------------

### 1. Get all tickets from MongoDB
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets


### 2. Get one ticket by ID
# IMPORTANT: Run the "Get all tickets" request above first. 
# Look at the JSON response, copy the 24-character "id", and replace YOUR_REAL_TICKET_ID below!
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/YOUR_REAL_TICKET_ID


### 3. Get missing ticket (Should return 404 Not Found)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/000000000000000000000000

### 4. Create a valid ticket (Day 7 Exercise 4)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Cannot access email",
  "description": "User cannot login to company email account.",
  "category": "Email",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "createdBy": "amir@example.com"
}


### 5. Create an invalid ticket (Should return 400 Bad Request)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "",
  "category": "",
  "priority": "",
  "createdBy": ""
}

### Get all tickets (No filters)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets

### Filter tickets by Status
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets?status=OPEN

### Filter tickets by Priority
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets?priority=HIGH

### Filter tickets by Category
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets?category=Email

### Get paginated tickets (Page 0, Default sorting)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=5

### Get paginated tickets (Page 1)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/paged?page=1&size=5

### Get paginated tickets (Custom sort: CreatedAt Descending)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=5&sortBy=createdAt&direction=desc
